; A standalone interval allocator: given a script of allocations and frees
; (keys, byte sizes and alignments only), it places every block at an aligned
; offset in one pool so that blocks live at the same time never overlap, and
; it can prove a placement correct with its own witness check. It knows
; nothing about tensors, kinds or Bigarrays; the client makes one problem per
; pool. See .ai/ (the tensor arena design).
;
; Depends on [core] (for its byte quantities), [err_trace] and [fmt] only, so
; `dune build lib/interval_alloc` proves the boundary. It is reachable from
; js_of_ocaml, hence sizes and offsets are [int64]-backed throughout: nothing
; here assumes a 63-bit [int].
;
; Wrapped (default): consumers see [Interval_alloc.Script] and so on. The
; [Ia_*] modules are the implementation behind the one public module.

(library
 (name interval_alloc)
 (private_modules
  ia_check
  ia_decode
  ia_reference
  ia_script
  ia_search
  ia_solution
  ia_strategy)
 (libraries core err_trace fmt))
